      "line": 189,
      "verdict": "verified in exact local source",
      "hypothesis_translation": "The p-adic integers form the closed norm-at-most-one subset of the complete p-adic field; its inherited uniform structure is complete."
    },
    {
      "path": "Mathlib/NumberTheory/Padics/PadicIntegers.lean",
      "sha256": "5392888b7e9833f14ab600bd3a3944da1f341366da2f3de95cd9737a19b1ff3b",
      "declaration": "PadicInt.exists_pow_neg_lt",
      "line": 266,
      "verdict": "verified in exact local source",
      "hypothesis_translation": "For any positive real epsilon, p to a sufficiently negative integer power is smaller. Primality supplies p>1; p=2 is included."
    },
    {
      "path": "Mathlib/NumberTheory/Padics/PadicIntegers.lean",
      "sha256": "5392888b7e9833f14ab600bd3a3944da1f341366da2f3de95cd9737a19b1ff3b",
      "declaration": "PadicInt.norm_int_le_pow_iff_dvd",
      "line": 290,
      "verdict": "verified in exact local source",
      "hypothesis_translation": "An integer cast has p-adic norm at most p^(-n) exactly when p^n divides it in the integers."
    },
    {
      "path": "Mathlib/NumberTheory/Padics/PadicIntegers.lean",
      "sha256": "5392888b7e9833f14ab600bd3a3944da1f341366da2f3de95cd9737a19b1ff3b",
      "declaration": "PadicInt.norm_le_pow_iff_mem_span_pow",
      "line": 473,
      "verdict": "verified in exact local source",
      "hypothesis_translation": "A p-adic value has norm at most p^(-n) exactly when it lies in the ideal generated by p^n. This is the retained-precision condition."
    },
    {
      "path": "Mathlib/NumberTheory/Padics/RingHoms.lean",
